            <ArticleTitle>Diabetes mellitus and cardiovascular clinical characteristics of Spanish women with stable ischaemic heart disease: Data from the SIRENA study.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>82-86</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0168-8227(16)30427-2</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.diabres.2016.11.019</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The relationship between diabetes and the cardiovascular clinical characteristics of Spanish women with stable ischaemic heart disease was studied in a nationwide cross-sectional study. Diabetes was related to a higher burden of risk factors, comorbidity, multivessel disease and coronary surgery.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright © 2016 Elsevier Ireland Ltd. All rights reserved.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
